drm/i915/dp: Read an eDP panel's SDP caps when it's set up

Whether the sink takes the Adaptive-Sync SDP is only read in
intel_dp_detect(), and the first detect comes after the initial commit
the driver makes while it loads. On an eDP panel that can do VRR, that
commit computes a state without the SDP, and the next one, the fbdev
console's, with it. infoframes.enable then differs in a bit the fastset
check only ignores while VRR is enabled, so the console's commit is a
second full modeset, with the panel's power cycle, about 1.1 s dark.

intel_edp_init_dpcd() already reads the eDP panel's DPCD and its DSC
caps, so read the SDP caps there too. intel_dp_detect() still reads them
again, as it does the DSC caps.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
@@ -4889,6 +4889,8 @@
 	intel_edp_set_data_override_rates(intel_dp);
 }
 
+static void intel_dp_detect_sdp_caps(struct intel_dp *intel_dp);
+
 static bool
 intel_edp_init_dpcd(struct intel_dp *intel_dp, struct intel_connector *connector)
 {
@@ -4957,6 +4959,13 @@
 	/* Read the eDP DSC DPCD registers */
 	intel_dp_detect_dsc_caps(intel_dp, connector);
 
+	/*
+	 * And the SDP caps, so the state computed before the first detect,
+	 * as the initial commit's is, has the Adaptive-Sync SDP the next
+	 * commit's will, and that commit can be a fastset.
+	 */
+	intel_dp_detect_sdp_caps(intel_dp);
+
 	return true;
 }
 
